  "summary": "Typosquat package exfiltrates host identifiers to hardcoded webhook.site collector",
  "details": "vercel-runtime-python@99.99.99 is a typosquat-shaped package (name mimics Vercel, version 99.99.99) whose only shipped functionality is a send_info() function exposed at top level via __init__.py. When invoked, it collects the installer's hostname, resolved IP address, operating system and machine architecture and POSTs them as JSON to a hardcoded anonymous request-inspection endpoint at https://webhook.site/f9bff304-3053-4d54-be05-86537267514a. The destination is not caller-configurable, and the package provides no other legitimate functionality that would justify contacting a third-party collector. Any consumer that imports and uses the package's public API leaks host reconnaissance data to an author-controlled endpoint.",
